      "question": "<p>In this question you must show all stages of your working.</p><p>Solutions relying on calculator technology are not acceptable.</p><p>A particle is moving along a straight line.</p><p>At time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> seconds, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t &gt; 0\"></span>, the velocity of the particle is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v \\text{ m s}^{-1}\"></span>, where</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"v = 2t - 7\\sqrt{t} + 6\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>(a) Find the acceleration of the particle when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t = 4\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t = 1\"></span> the particle is at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"X\"></span>.</p><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t = 2\"></span> the particle is at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Y\"></span>.</p><p>Given that the particle does not come to instantaneous rest in the interval <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1 &lt; t &lt; 2\"></span></p><p>(b) show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"XY = \\frac{1}{3}\\left(41 - 28\\sqrt{2}\\right)\"></span> metres.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p>",
