      "question": "<p>[In this question, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf i\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf j\"></span> are perpendicular unit vectors in a horizontal plane.]</p><p>A particle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> is moving on a smooth horizontal surface under the action of two forces.</p><p>Given that</p><ul><li>the mass of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> is 2 kg</li></ul><ul><li>the two forces are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2\\mathbf i + 4\\mathbf j)N\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(c\\mathbf i - 2\\mathbf j)N\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span> is a constant</li></ul><ul><li>the magnitude of the acceleration of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{5} \\text{ m s}^{-2}\"></span></li></ul><p>find the two possible values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p>",
