      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-22-2024-june/q4",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:136mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-22-2024-june/q04-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 2. Car towing a trailer on a horizontal road.\"></figure><p>Figure 2 shows a car towing a trailer along a straight horizontal road.</p><p>The mass of the car is 800 kg and the mass of the trailer is 600 kg.</p><p>The trailer is attached to the car by a towbar which is parallel to the road and parallel to the direction of motion of the car and the trailer.</p><p>The towbar is modelled as a light rod.</p><p>The resistance to the motion of the car is modelled as a constant force of magnitude 400 N.</p><p>The resistance to the motion of the trailer is modelled as a constant force of magnitude <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span> newtons.</p><p>The engine of the car is producing a constant driving force that is horizontal and of magnitude 1740 N.</p><p>The acceleration of the car is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.6 \\text{ m s}^{-2}\"></span> and the tension in the towbar is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span> newtons.</p><p>Using the model,</p><p>(a) show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R = 500\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>(b) find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>At the instant when the speed of the car and the trailer is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"12.5 \\text{ m s}^{-1}\"></span>, the towbar breaks.</p><p>The trailer moves a further distance <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d\"></span> metres before coming to rest.</p><p>The resistance to the motion of the trailer is modelled as a constant force of magnitude 500 N.</p><p>Using the model,</p><p>(c) show that, after the towbar breaks, the deceleration of the trailer is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{5}{6} \\text{ m s}^{-2}\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p>(d) find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>In reality, the distance <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d\"></span> metres is likely to be different from the answer found in part (d).</p><p>(e) Give two different reasons why this is the case.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p>",
